# SDD ledger — plan: .superpowers/sdd/2026-08-25-price-loop-diagnosis/plan.md

## Setup and preflight

- Existing branch is `codex/pit-canslim-strategy-diagnosis` at `33a5fde`.
- The working tree was clean before this plan.
- The existing PIT bundle and compact fundamentals are the only inputs in scope.
- No tests, downloads, optimizer calls, or shared-branch writes are permitted.

### Task/interface scan

| Task | Interface | Finding / ruling |
|---|---|---|
| 1 -> 2 | bounded diagnostics -> engine change | The audit must prove a timing/coverage defect before implementation; thresholds remain unchanged. |
| 2 -> 3 | engine change -> replay output | The replay must report signal, execution, rejection, and cash counters from the same result object. |
| 1 -> 3 | data coverage -> selected universe | The verification universe must be explicit and bounded; do not infer full S&P coverage from 12 tickers. |

### Ruling

- Ruling: treat same-day volume and evaluation cadence as separate hypotheses — collapsing them would hide whether misses come from confirmation semantics or from sampling every fifth session; cost if wrong is one additional bounded diagnostic run.

Task 2: implementer completed in the working tree (base `33a5fde`); report
counts immutable entry-attempt outcomes without changing engine behavior.
Task 2: task review dispatched for the additive report diff; commit remains
pending because the sandbox denied `.git/index.lock` creation.
Task 2: complete (commit `734647a`, review PASS/APPROVED; no findings).

Task 1: bounded read-only audits completed. The bundle has 866,025 price rows
for 607 symbols, 99.971% active-member/session coverage, and complete history
for the selected 12 leaders. Five-day sampling produced 40 signals; daily
sampling produced 103 signals and 81 executions, with zero cash/capacity/risk
rejections. This supports cadence as the first-order opportunity issue, not a
price-coverage or SEC-data issue. Exact daily artifacts/output capture remains
the verification step.

Task 3: bounded daily replay completed by the price-loop runner at
`equity_curve_20260825_172557.csv`: 103 signals, 81 executions, 22
next-open buy-zone rejections, and zero cash/capacity/risk rejections. A
post-commit one-symbol daily replay verified the new report section and showed
`entries_executed: 3` plus `entry_rejected_next_open_buy_zone: 1`.

Ruling: keep the 1.30x same-day volume confirmation unchanged for CANSLIM
fidelity; make daily evaluation the diagnostic default for PIT callers rather
than weakening the volume rule. Cost if wrong: a later strategy diagnosis may
need to revisit volume semantics, but changing it now would conflate timing
with fidelity.

Task 3: complete (bounded replay and report verification complete; no further
engine change required in this pass).

Leader-recall follow-up: the existing corrected full PIT replay reports
50/100 raw five-year leaders signaled and 47/100 executed (42/72 and 40/72
for members present at the start), with a 65.06% mechanical leader basket
versus -9.99% CANSLIM and 84.79% SPY. The bounded 14-name daily technical
cohort on bundle `8d5bdca9...` produced 165 signals and 138 executions, with
78.2% average cash and no cash/capacity/risk blocks. This cohort result is
diagnostic only because it is selected from ex-post leaders.

Leader-recall artifact: `.artifacts/backtests/technical_only_non_pit_exposure_aware_leader_recall.csv` and `.json`; explicitly labeled non-PIT-exposure-aware.

Task 4: coverage audit and documented C/A fallback repair are in progress. The
bounded artifact audit identified existing PIT rows where a preferred EPS row
is present but has no latest as-of comparison while Net Income is available;
the implementation is limited to selecting the documented fallback row and
does not relax any CANSLIM threshold or add data.

Task 4: implementation complete (`2578552..2164b61`). The task reviewer
returned Spec PASS and Task quality APPROVED after the report was amended with
baseline-versus-current probe evidence; scoped re-review returned ADDRESSED
with no new breakage.

Ruling: use the existing normalized Net Income fallback when the preferred EPS
row lacks a latest as-of comparison, while preserving invalid-growth fail-closed
semantics — this repairs a documented evaluator contract without importing
external data; cost if wrong is a bounded change in C/A availability that must
be rechecked against the next replay.

Ruling: replace the rolling-high pivot only in strict, validated PIT
fundamental runs; retain the two-argument/technical-only compatibility path —
this enforces the hard CANSLIM proper-base requirement without changing legacy
diagnostic behavior; cost if wrong is reduced strict-PIT recall until the
pattern policy is refined, which is measurable in the next bounded replay.

Task 5: implementation complete in commit `ab068de`; task review is pending.
The requested six-symbol replay was stopped after ten minutes with no output
and no artifacts; the implementer used a one-symbol 2024 strict-PIT replay
instead (24 signal rows, zero attempts/executions/rejections).

Task 5: complete (`ab068de..a1449a0`, review clean). The scoped re-review
returned ADDRESSED, Spec PASS, and Task quality APPROVED after the report
recorded the one-symbol 2023–2025 strict-PIT replay (666 evaluated rows, 3
signals/attempts, 2 executions, 1 next-open buy-zone rejection, no crash).

Final review: the broad whole-branch reviewer was interrupted after two
bounded waits without returning a verdict. Direct `git diff --check` was clean,
the focused Task 4 and Task 5 reviews were clean, and no additional source
changes were made. This is a review-process limitation, not a code finding.
